<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Corpus de Sang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1640</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reapers-war">Reapers' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Corpus de Sang ('Bloody Corpus') was the riot of 7 June 1640 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>, when reapers and townspeople, angered by the billeting of royal troops, killed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmau-de-queralt-count-of-santa-coloma">Count of Santa Coloma</a>. It began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reapers-war">Reapers' War</a>, the Catalan revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-iv-of-spain">Philip IV of Spain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/corpus-de-sang.jpg" alt="Corpus de Sang" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hermenegildo Miralles - (print in the public domain... is more than 100 years old &amp;amp; author died more then 70 year... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Els_segadors.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
